@startuml system-workflow
title TestEase Usage Tracker — Workflow (Test Ease reports raw events; an admin views the dashboard)

skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam roundcorner 8
skinparam ArrowColor #444444
skinparam ArrowFontColor #333333
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #FFF7E0
skinparam NoteBorderColor #E0C46C

actor "User" as User

participant "nginx\n(SPA + /api proxy)" as NGINX #E8F5E9
participant "FastAPI api\n(ingestion + dashboard)" as API #E3F2FD

database "PostgreSQL\n(4 raw event tables)" as DB #ECEFF1
boundary  "Test Ease\n(usage reporter)"  as TE #ECEFF1

== Step 1 — Test Ease reports the events since its checkpoint ==
TE -> API : POST /events (X-API-Key)\nper-action events for jane@…
activate API
API -> API : validate **each row**;\nbad rows → `rejected`
API -> DB : bulk INSERT per event type\n**ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING**
API --> TE : 200 — accepted counts + rejected[]
deactivate API

== Step 2 — The admin opens the dashboard ==
User -> NGINX : GET / (dashboard :3005)
NGINX --> User : **React SPA** (login screen — no token yet)

== Step 3 — Login mints a 12h session token ==
User -> NGINX : POST /api/dashboard/login
NGINX -> API : /dashboard/login (prefix stripped)
activate API
API -> API : verify credentials,\nmint **HMAC token** (12h expiry)
API --> NGINX : { token, expires_at }
deactivate API
NGINX --> User : token → localStorage

== Step 4 — Fetch aggregated stats ==
User -> NGINX : GET /api/dashboard/summary?from&to\n(Authorization: Bearer)
NGINX -> API : /dashboard/summary
activate API
API -> API : verify token HMAC + expiry
API -> DB : COUNT per event table,\nCOUNT DISTINCT users, GROUP BY day
DB --> API : aggregate rows
API --> NGINX : **StatsSummary / DailyStats** JSON
deactivate API
NGINX --> User : 📊 dashboard data

== Step 5 — Render ==
User -> User : render **KPI tiles + SVG activity chart**

note across
  Test Ease sends **one row per action** on an interval — not daily totals —
  batched since its own checkpoint, and each row is a plain append-only INSERT.
  Every total on the dashboard is derived by grouping those rows at query time.
  The dashboard never queries Postgres directly: it reads aggregates through
  the same FastAPI service, behind nginx's /api proxy and an HMAC session token.
end note

@enduml
